      "text": "## BFS vs DFS — The Core Contrast"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TRAVERSAL.md#009",
      "path": [
        "02-TRAVERSAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:02-traversal, git-history:graph-algorithms:02-traversal]",
        "canonical_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "concepts": "[BFS, DFS, topological sort, connected components, cycle detection]",
        "current_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:graph-algorithms:traversal",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "graph-algorithms",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[graph traversal]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Graph Traversal",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Property | BFS | DFS |\n|----------|-----|-----|\n| Frontier | queue (FIFO) | stack / recursion (LIFO) |\n| Order | by distance (layers) | by depth (dive then backtrack) |\n| Time | O(V+E) | O(V+E) |\n| Space | O(V) — worst frontier is a full layer | O(V) — recursion depth ≤ V |\n| Finds | **fewest-edges** shortest path (unweighted) | a spanning tree; finish-time order |\n| Natural for | shortest hops, level structure, bipartite test | topo sort, SCC, cycle detect, backtracking |\n| Implicit-graph use | uniform-cost frontier search | iterative deepening, game trees |"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TRAVERSAL.md#010",
      "path": [
        "02-TRAVERSAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:02-traversal, git-history:graph-algorithms:02-traversal]",
        "canonical_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "concepts": "[BFS, DFS, topological sort, connected components, cycle detection]",
        "current_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:graph-algorithms:traversal",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "graph-algorithms",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[graph traversal]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Graph Traversal",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "> BFS gives shortest paths **only when every edge has the same cost** (hop count).\n> The moment edges carry weights, BFS is wrong and you escalate to Dijkstra\n> (`03`) — which is, structurally, BFS with a priority queue replacing the plain\n> queue."
    },
    {
