      "text": "## DFS — The DFS Tree and Edge Classification"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TRAVERSAL.md#020",
      "path": [
        "02-TRAVERSAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:02-traversal, git-history:graph-algorithms:02-traversal]",
        "canonical_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "concepts": "[BFS, DFS, topological sort, connected components, cycle detection]",
        "current_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:graph-algorithms:traversal",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "graph-algorithms",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[graph traversal]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Graph Traversal",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "DFS dives as deep as possible before backtracking. Its real value is the\n*structure* it exposes: a DFS forest plus a classification of every edge, which\nis the substrate for topo sort, SCCs, bridges, and cycle detection."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TRAVERSAL.md#021",
      "path": [
        "02-TRAVERSAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:02-traversal, git-history:graph-algorithms:02-traversal]",
        "canonical_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "concepts": "[BFS, DFS, topological sort, connected components, cycle detection]",
        "current_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:graph-algorithms:traversal",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "graph-algorithms",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[graph traversal]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Graph Traversal",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  Directed graph, DFS from 0:        Edge types relative to the DFS tree:\n                                     ------------------------------------\n     0 ---> 1 ---> 2                 TREE  : edge to a freshly-discovered\n     |      ^      |                         vertex (0->1, 1->2)\n     v      |      v                 BACK  : edge to a GRAY ancestor  => CYCLE\n     3 -----+      4                         (2->1 here) <-- proves a cycle\n                                     FWD   : edge to a BLACK descendant\n   discover/finish times:           CROSS : edge to a finished vertex in\n     0: d=1            f=10                  another subtree\n     1: d=2  3: d=3 f=4\n     2: d=5  4: d=6 f=7 f=8 f=9      In an UNDIRECTED graph: only TREE and\n                                     BACK edges exist (no fwd/cross).\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TRAVERSAL.md#022",
      "path": [
        "02-TRAVERSAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:02-traversal, git-history:graph-algorithms:02-traversal]",
