      "text": "## Topological Sort — Ordering a DAG"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-TRAVERSAL.md#027",
      "path": [
        "02-TRAVERSAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:graph-algorithms:02-traversal, git-history:graph-algorithms:02-traversal]",
        "canonical_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "concepts": "[BFS, DFS, topological sort, connected components, cycle detection]",
        "current_path": "graph-algorithms/02-TRAVERSAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:graph-algorithms:traversal",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "graph-algorithms",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[graph traversal]",
        "section": "mathematics-physics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Graph Traversal",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A topological order lists the vertices of a **DAG** (directed *acyclic* graph) so\nthat every edge points forward. It is the formal model of \"do prerequisites\nfirst\": build dependencies, course prerequisites, task scheduling, package\ninstall order. **A topo order exists iff the graph is acyclic** — a cycle is a\nmutual dependency with no valid order."
    }
